    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "a2317bc9_4680db4d",
        "filename": "zephyr/drivers/usbc/pdc_rts54xx.c",
        "patchSetId": 30
      },
      "lineNbr": 2200,
      "author": {
        "id": 1106949
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-04-24T19:23:16Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e This duplicates code in the driver and subsystem. Is there a reason why this needs to be done?\n\nrts54_execute_command is a blocking command executer. (Renamed to rts54_execute_command_sync.) It allows a PDC driver not to worry about how to route a CC event back to the caller. uPPM also works with blocking smbus APIs. \n\n\u003e I haven\u0027t reviewed the full CL stack. How is synchronization between pdc_power_mgmt.c and the ucsi/rts54xx.c driver managed?\n\nPDM isn\u0027t supposed to use rts54_execute_command. When PDM is accessing a PDC, PPM will get -EBUSY and when PPM is accessing a PDC, PDM will get -EBUSY.\n\n\u003e public_api_block in pdc_power_mgmt.c is already setup to generate a blocking PDC command.\n\nThat was explored as the serial architecture described in https://docs.google.com/document/d/1pNZuFHzxrFhKH3xy1_F61dySB9c9Ttu4IZRPhD8KmNA/edit?resourcekey\u003d0-JBLbWckIUZyPMwb3PbOYtw\u0026tab\u003dt.0#bookmark\u003did.h79q0zj86q07. An observation is transitioning to the final architecture from the parallel architecture is more seamless than transitioning from the serial architecture: https://docs.google.com/document/d/1pNZuFHzxrFhKH3xy1_F61dySB9c9Ttu4IZRPhD8KmNA/edit?resourcekey\u003d0-JBLbWckIUZyPMwb3PbOYtw\u0026tab\u003dt.0#bookmark\u003did.5qbxnvh3gfr1.",
      "parentUuid": "257cd2e1_019bf8e5",
